    "summary": "High-energy show with smoking Bird Song & 30‑min Playing In The Band",
    "blurb": "Features a searing Bird Song, an expansive 30‑minute Playing In The Band, and strong renditions of Candyman, Box of Rain and Brokedown Palace. Jerry’s pre‑effects Strat tone and Keith’s jazzy keyboards drive the high‑energy performance while Billy provides solid rhythmic support.",
    "review": "The November 15, 1972 concert at Oklahoma City Music Hall captures the Dead in top form, riding a wave of relentless momentum that only a late‑'70s lineup could sustain. The first set builds with a smoking Bird Song and an inventive Candyman before slipping into a tight groove on Box of Rain; Phil’s relaxed bass lines sit perfectly beneath Jerry’s crystal‑clear Strat work. The second set erupts into a monster Playing In The Band that stretches beyond thirty minutes, where Keith Godchaux’s jazzy keyboard textures intertwine with Jerry’s loopy solo and Billy Kreutzmann’s driving drums, creating an explosive yet cohesive jam. Highlights like Brokedown Palace, Cumberland Blues, Big Railroad Blues, Me And Bobby McGee and Wharf Rat showcase the band’s melodic depth and rhythmic tightness, while the encore Johnny B. Goode caps a night that feels both expansive and intimate. The Miller soundboard source (gd1972-11-15.sbd.miller.110631.flac16) presents this performance with crystal‑clear separation and low noise, making every nuance of the band’s interplay audible and vivid.",
